<%# Shown at the foot of every page to members of a fixed-list club who haven't
    uploaded their watch history, until they do or they dismiss it. Those clubs
    skip films any of you has already seen, and without this we only know what
    they've logged lately — so the ballot keeps offering films people watched
    years ago. %>
<section class="onboarding import-prompt">
  <form method="post" action="/import/dismiss" class="dismiss">
    <%== csrf_tag("/import/dismiss") %>
    <input type="hidden" name="to" value="<%= path %>">
    <button type="submit" class="link" aria-label="Dismiss this reminder">&times;</button>
  </form>

  <h2>Tell us what you've seen</h2>
  <p>You're in a club that draws from a fixed list, so it skips films any of you
     has already watched. Letterboxd only tells us what you've logged lately, and
     the rest of your history has to come from their export &mdash; otherwise the
     ballot will keep offering you films you saw years ago.</p>
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Open <a href="https://letterboxd.com/user/exportdata/" target="_blank">letterboxd.com/user/exportdata/</a>
        and press <strong>Export your data</strong>. It arrives as a zip.</li>
    <li>Unzip it. Inside is <strong>watched.csv</strong> &mdash; that's the one.
        (<code>watchlist.csv</code> is films you want to see; we already read those.)</li>
    <li><a href="/settings#import">Upload it on your settings page</a>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="dim">We keep the film names and nothing else &mdash; no dates, no ratings, no reviews.</p>
</section>
